// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Support Tickets
// screen (project/AdminTickets.dc.html -> NavSidebar role="admin"
// active="Support tickets" + the plain shared NavTop.astro
// (section="Manage" page="Support tickets") + PageSupportQueue — NOT
// PageTickets.dc.html, a different, list+detail split-pane component
// that AdminTickets.dc.html does not import (that one belongs to the
// already-approved Inventory Staff Support Ticket screen). This is a
// genuinely separate Admin-shell screen — no markup reused from Customer
// Support, Customer Support Ticket, or Inventory Staff Support Tickets,
// per your explicit instruction.
//
// SCOPE: this is the ticket QUEUE (list) only.
//
// LINKING (this turn): Admin Ticket Detail (/admin/tickets/[id]) now
// exists, so each real ticket row links there — per your own explicit
// instruction once that screen shipped ("It is now appropriate for
// /admin/tickets ticket rows to link to the new Admin Ticket Detail
// route"). The design's trailing "..." row-actions button is still
// omitted entirely (no real per-row action exists on this screen that
// isn't just "open the ticket").
//
// SCHEMA REALITY vs THE DESIGN: support_tickets has exactly nine real
// columns — id, created_by, assigned_to, subject, description, status,
// resolution, created_at, updated_at (confirmed live). There is no
// category/priority/order_id/SLA/messages/attachments/internal-notes
// table anywhere in this schema (confirmed — matches your own explicit
// list of what this model does NOT contain). The design's "Category"
// table column is still omitted outright for the same reason (no real
// concept exists at all, unlike a physical bin location that's simply
// untracked). The "Category" FACET, however, is now reproduced visually
// (per your follow-up refinement) as a real, honestly disabled control —
// present in the toolbar for fidelity, but `disabled` with a title
// explaining why, never pretending to filter.
//
// FILTER REFINEMENT (this turn): re-added the design's own dedicated
// toolbar search box (was previously only reachable via NavTop's shared
// search — both now wired to the same real `search` query param, same
// dual-search-entry-point precedent already established on Admin
// Customers), added a real "+ Status" compact facet (alongside the
// already-real status tabs — intentionally redundant with them, matching
// the design's own toolbar exactly, both driving the same real `status`
// param), and made "+ Assignee" unconditionally visible with a real
// "Unassigned" option (assigned_to IS NULL) rather than only appearing
// once a ticket happens to be assigned.
//
// Real vs deferred/fabricated, per your explicit no-fabrication rules:
//  - Real: every ticket row (support_tickets_select_admin — admin/
//    super_admin see every ticket, unscoped, unlike inventory_staff who
//    only ever sees tickets assigned to them), real id, real subject,
//    real status across the full real 5-value ticket_status enum (open/
//    in_progress/waiting/resolved/closed — confirmed live, maps exactly
//    onto the design's own 5 status labels, no invented or dropped
//    values), real created_by (joined to profiles — customer requesters
//    shown by name; staff/admin requesters shown "Internal · {name}",
//    matching the design's own exact convention, driven by the real
//    profiles.role of the creator, not a guess), real assigned_to (joined
//    to profiles — "Unassigned" when null, the real assignee's name
//    otherwise), real updated_at (Today/HH:MM or D MMM, same compact
//    convention the design itself uses). Real search (matches real
//    subject or real ticket id), real status tabs AND a real "+ Status"
//    facet with real counts (both drive the same real status param),
//    real "+ Assignee" facet — named options derived only from staff who
//    are actually assigned to at least one real ticket (empty in the
//    live data today since 0 real tickets are assigned yet, same "derive
//    facet options from data actually present" convention used on every
//    other Admin screen) plus a real "Unassigned" option backed by the
//    real assigned_to IS NULL state.
//  - Stat strip — all 4 real, computed from the same real ticket set:
//    "Open" (real count) + real "{N} unassigned" note (open AND
//    assigned_to is null); "In Progress" (real count) + note "store-wide"
//    (the design's own "with inventory staff" note assumes every
//    in-progress ticket is assigned to inventory staff specifically —
//    assigned_to has no role constraint at the database level, so that
//    wasn't asserted as fact); "Waiting" (real count) — the design's own
//    "on customer reply" note assumes a specific reason no field actually
//    records, so dropped rather than asserted; "Resolved this week" (real
//    count of resolved-or-closed tickets with a real updated_at in the
//    real last-7-IST-days window, via the same shared
//    resolveDashboardRange("7d") IST-safe helper already used on Admin
//    Stock/Product Info/every other dashboard in this project).
//  - Header subtitle: the design's own copy ("...reply, assign to
//    inventory staff and resolve") names three actions — replying and
//    assigning have no real write path from this screen this turn
//    (updateSupportTicket only ever touches status/resolution, never
//    assigned_to; no message/reply table exists at all) — dropped to a
//    plain, honest "Customer and internal tickets in one queue".
//  - Checkboxes + bulk actions: no real bulk ticket action exists —
//    omitted, same "do not invent bulk actions" precedent as every other
//    Admin list screen.
//  - "View" grid/list toggle: omitted, no view-mode capability exists.
//  - Footer pagination ("Page 1 of 1"): replaced with a real "{N} of {M}
//    tickets" count, same precedent as every other Admin list screen.
//
// ADMIN CAPABILITIES CHECKED AND DELIBERATELY NOT BUILT THIS TURN:
// updateSupportTicket() only ever sets status/resolution, never
// assigned_to — even though support_tickets_update_admin's own RLS would
// technically permit admin to update assigned_to via a raw table write,
// no Action/RPC exists that does so, so no "Assign" control was added
// anywhere (matches your explicit "do not invent ticket assignment if the
// current action/schema cannot actually persist it"). Status/resolution
// updates themselves belong to the ticket detail view (next turn), not
// this queue/list screen — the design's own PageSupportQueue.dc.html has
// no inline status-change control either.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";
import { resolveDashboardRange } from "../../../lib/dashboardRange";

const url = Astro.url;
const search = url.searchParams.get("search")?.trim() ?? "";
const status = url.searchParams.get("status") ?? "";
const assignee = url.searchParams.get("assignee") ?? "";
const viewerRole = (Astro.locals.role === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

// --- Real full ticket queue (support_tickets_select_admin — unscoped) ---
const { data: ticketRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("support_tickets")
  .select("id, subject, status, created_by, assigned_to, updated_at")
  .order("updated_at", { ascending: false });

const tickets = ticketRows ?? [];

const profileIds = [...new Set(tickets.flatMap((t) => [t.created_by, t.assigned_to].filter((id): id is string => Boolean(id))))];
const { data: profileRows } =
  profileIds.length > 0
    ? await Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id, full_name, role").in("id", profileIds)
    : { data: [] };
const profileById = new Map((profileRows ?? []).map((p) => [p.id, { name: p.full_name ?? "Unnamed", role: p.role as string }]));

const STATUS_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
  open: "Open",
  in_progress: "In Progress",
  waiting: "Waiting",
  resolved: "Resolved",
  closed: "Closed",
};
const STATUS_TONE: Record<string, "outline" | "info" | "warn" | "success" | "muted"> = {
  open: "outline",
  in_progress: "info",
  waiting: "warn",
  resolved: "success",
  closed: "muted",
};
const ALL_STATUSES = ["open", "in_progress", "waiting", "resolved", "closed"] as const;

function formatUpdated(iso: string): string {
  const d = new Date(iso);
  const now = new Date();
  const IST_OFFSET_MS = 5.5 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  const dIst = new Date(d.getTime() + IST_OFFSET_MS);
  const nowIst = new Date(now.getTime() + IST_OFFSET_MS);
  const sameIstDay =
    dIst.getUTCFullYear() === nowIst.getUTCFullYear() && dIst.getUTCMonth() === nowIst.getUTCMonth() && dIst.getUTCDate() === nowIst.getUTCDate();
  if (sameIstDay) return `Today, ${d.toLocaleTimeString(undefined, { hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit" })}`;
  return d.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short" });
}

const allRows = tickets.map((t) => {
  const creator = profileById.get(t.created_by);
  const isInternalCreator = creator ? creator.role !== "customer" : false;
  return {
    id: t.id as string,
    subject: t.subject as string,
    status: t.status as string,
    requesterLabel: creator ? (isInternalCreator ? `Internal · ${creator.name}` : creator.name) : "—",
    isInternalCreator,
    assigneeId: t.assigned_to as string | null,
    assigneeName: t.assigned_to ? (profileById.get(t.assigned_to)?.name ?? "—") : null,
    updatedAt: t.updated_at as string,
    updatedLabel: formatUpdated(t.updated_at as string),
  };
});

// --- Real status tabs ---
const statusCounts = new Map<string, number>(ALL_STATUSES.map((s) => [s, 0]));
for (const t of allRows) statusCounts.set(t.status, (statusCounts.get(t.status) ?? 0) + 1);
const TABS: { key: string; label: string }[] = [
  { key: "", label: "All" },
  { key: "open", label: "Open" },
  { key: "in_progress", label: "In Progress" },
  { key: "waiting", label: "Waiting" },
  { key: "resolved", label: "Resolved" },
  { key: "closed", label: "Closed" },
];

// --- Real "Assignee" facet (only staff actually assigned to at least one
// real ticket, plus a real "Unassigned" option backed by the real null
// state — not derived data, but always offered since it's a genuine,
// always-meaningful value for this field) ---
const assigneeOptions = [...new Map(allRows.filter((t) => t.assigneeId).map((t) => [t.assigneeId!, t.assigneeName!])).entries()]
  .map(([id, name]) => ({ id, name }))
  .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const UNASSIGNED_SENTINEL = "unassigned";

// --- Real filter — search matches real subject or real ticket id (full
// or the same truncated 8-char prefix shown in the table) ---
const filtered = allRows.filter((t) => {
  if (status && t.status !== status) return false;
  if (assignee === UNASSIGNED_SENTINEL && t.assigneeId) return false;
  if (assignee && assignee !== UNASSIGNED_SENTINEL && t.assigneeId !== assignee) return false;
  if (!search) return true;
  const needle = search.toLowerCase();
  return t.subject.toLowerCase().includes(needle) || t.id.toLowerCase().includes(needle);
});

function buildUrl(overrides: Record<string, string | undefined>) {
  const next = new URLSearchParams(url.search);
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(overrides)) {
    if (value) next.set(key, value);
    else next.delete(key);
  }
  const qs = next.toString();
  return qs ? `/admin/tickets?${qs}` : "/admin/tickets";
}

// --- Real stat strip ---
const openCount = statusCounts.get("open") ?? 0;
const openUnassignedCount = allRows.filter((t) => t.status === "open" && !t.assigneeId).length;
const inProgressCount = statusCounts.get("in_progress") ?? 0;
const waitingCount = statusCounts.get("waiting") ?? 0;

const sevenDayRange = resolveDashboardRange("7d");
const resolvedThisWeekCount = allRows.filter(
  (t) => (t.status === "resolved" || t.status === "closed") && new Date(t.updatedAt) >= new Date(sevenDayRange.from!)
).length;

const stats = [
  { label: "Open", value: String(openCount), note: `${openUnassignedCount} unassigned` },
  { label: "In Progress", value: String(inProgressCount), note: "store-wide" },
  { label: "Waiting", value: String(waitingCount), note: "" },
  { label: "Resolved this week", value: String(resolvedThisWeekCount), note: "" },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Support tickets — Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Support tickets" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Manage" page="Support tickets" searchAction="/admin/tickets" searchName="search" searchValue={search} searchPlaceholder="Search tickets…" />

      <main id="main-content" class="tk__main">
        <div class="tk__header">
          <div class="tk__heading-col">
            <h1>Support tickets</h1>
            <span class="tk__subtitle">Customer and internal tickets in one queue</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tk__stats">
          {stats.map((s) => (
            <div class="tk__stat-card">
              <span class="tk__stat-label">{s.label}</span>
              <div class="tk__stat-body">
                <span class="tk__stat-value">{s.value}</span>
                {s.note && <span class="tk__stat-note">{s.note}</span>}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="tk__toolbar">
          <div role="tablist" aria-label="Ticket status" class="tk__tabs">
            {TABS.map((t) => (
              <a href={buildUrl({ status: t.key || undefined })} role="tab" aria-selected={status === t.key} class={status === t.key ? "is-active" : ""}>
                {t.label} <span class="tk__tab-count">{t.key ? (statusCounts.get(t.key) ?? 0) : allRows.length}</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tk__toolbar">
          <form method="get" action="/admin/tickets" class="tk__search-form">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 11a7 7 0 1 0 14 0a7 7 0 1 0-14 0M20 20l-4-4"></path></svg>
            <input type="search" name="search" value={search} aria-label="Search tickets" placeholder="Search tickets…" class="tk__search-input" />
            {status && <input type="hidden" name="status" value={status} />}
            {assignee && <input type="hidden" name="assignee" value={assignee} />}
          </form>

          <select id="tk-status-filter" class="tk__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by status">
            <option value={buildUrl({ status: undefined })} selected={!status}>+ Status</option>
            {ALL_STATUSES.map((s) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ status: s })} selected={status === s}>{STATUS_LABEL[s]}</option>
            ))}
          </select>

          <button type="button" class="tk__facet-select tk__facet-select--disabled" disabled title="Not available — this schema has no ticket category field">
            + Category
          </button>

          <select id="tk-assignee-filter" class="tk__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by assignee">
            <option value={buildUrl({ assignee: undefined })} selected={!assignee}>+ Assignee</option>
            <option value={buildUrl({ assignee: UNASSIGNED_SENTINEL })} selected={assignee === UNASSIGNED_SENTINEL}>Unassigned</option>
            {assigneeOptions.map((a) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ assignee: a.id })} selected={assignee === a.id}>{a.name}</option>
            ))}
          </select>
        </div>

        {
          filtered.length > 0 ? (
            <div class="tk__panel">
              <div class="tk__grid tk__grid-head">
                <span>Ticket</span>
                <span>Requester</span>
                <span>Status</span>
                <span>Assignee</span>
                <span>Updated</span>
              </div>
              {filtered.map((t) => (
                <a href={`/admin/tickets/${t.id}`} class="tk__grid tk__row">
                  <span class="tk__ticket-cell">
                    <span class="tk__ticket-id">{t.id.slice(0, 8)}</span>
                    <span class="tk__ticket-subject">{t.subject}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class={`tk__requester-cell ${t.isInternalCreator ? "tk__requester-cell--internal" : ""}`}>{t.requesterLabel}</span>
                  <span><span class={`tk__pill tk__pill--${STATUS_TONE[t.status] ?? "muted"}`}>{STATUS_LABEL[t.status] ?? t.status}</span></span>
                  {t.assigneeName ? (
                    <span class="tk__assignee-cell">
                      <span class="tk__avatar">{t.assigneeName.split(" ").filter(Boolean).slice(0, 2).map((p: string) => p[0]!.toUpperCase()).join("")}</span>
                      {t.assigneeName}
                    </span>
                  ) : (
                    <span class="tk__muted-cell">Unassigned</span>
                  )}
                  <span class="tk__muted-cell tk__ellipsis">{t.updatedLabel}</span>
                </a>
              ))}
              <div class="tk__panel-footer">{filtered.length} of {allRows.length} ticket{allRows.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}</div>
            </div>
          ) : (
            <div class="tk__empty">
              <p class="tk__empty-title">No tickets found</p>
              <p class="tk__empty-body">Try a different search or filter.</p>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sd {
    --sd-shell: #fafafa;
    --sd-panel: #ffffff;
    --sd-card: #ffffff;
    --sd-fg: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-fg2: #404040;
    --sd-muted: #f5f5f5;
    --sd-muted-fg: #737373;
    --sd-border: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-input: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-primary: #171717;
    --sd-primary-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-success-bg: #ecfdf3;
    --sd-success-fg: #15803d;
    --sd-warn-bg: #fef3e2;
    --sd-warn-fg: #9a3412;
    --sd-danger-bg: #feecec;
    --sd-danger-fg: #b91c1c;
    --sd-info-bg: #eef2ff;
    --sd-info-fg: #3538cd;
    --sd-accent: #2b50e0;
    --sd-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    color-scheme: light;

    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font-family: "Geist", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sd[data-theme="dark"] {
    --sd-shell: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-panel: #0f0f0f;
    --sd-card: #171717;
    --sd-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-fg2: #d4d4d4;
    --sd-muted: #262626;
    --sd-muted-fg: #a3a3a3;
    --sd-border: #262626;
    --sd-input: #363636;
    --sd-primary: #fafafa;
    --sd-primary-fg: #171717;
    --sd-success-bg: #0f2a1c;
    --sd-success-fg: #4ade80;
    --sd-warn-bg: #2e1f0e;
    --sd-warn-fg: #fdba74;
    --sd-danger-bg: #2d1414;
    --sd-danger-fg: #f87171;
    --sd-info-bg: #1e2240;
    --sd-info-fg: #a5b4fc;
    --sd-accent: #6b8afb;
    --sd-shadow: none;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
  .sd__backdrop {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    z-index: 20;
  }
  .sd__sidebar {
    height: 100vh;
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__sidebar {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      z-index: 30;
      transform: translateX(-100%);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .sd__sidebar.is-open {
      transform: translateX(0);
    }
    .sd__backdrop.is-open {
      display: block;
    }
  }
  .sd__panel {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 8px 8px 8px 0;
    background: var(--sd-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__panel {
      margin: 8px;
    }
  }

  .tk__main {
    flex-grow: 1;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 24px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .tk__main {
      padding: 16px;
    }
  }

  .tk__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }
  .tk__heading-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .tk__heading-col h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .tk__subtitle {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }

  .tk__stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .tk__stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .tk__stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .tk__stat-card {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .tk__stat-label {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tk__stat-body {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .tk__stat-value {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .tk__stat-note {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }

  .tk__toolbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tk__tabs {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 3px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--sd-muted);
    gap: 2px;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .tk__tabs a {
    height: 30px;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .tk__tabs a.is-active {
    background: var(--sd-card);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
  }
  .tk__tab-count {
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-left: 4px;
  }
  .tk__tabs a.is-active .tk__tab-count {
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tk__facet-select {
    height: 34px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--sd-input);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .tk__facet-select--disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tk__search-form {
    width: 260px;
    height: 34px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .tk__search-input {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 0;
    outline: 0;
